  "content": "Floods and landslides obstruct roads at 19 locations in Koshi and Bagmati Provinces\nOnlinekhabar\nMonday, October 6, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 6\nDue to\nfloods and landslides\n, roads have been completely blocked at 19 locations across Koshi and Bagmati provinces, 8 in Koshi and 11 in Bagmati.\nIn Koshi Province, several sections of the Koshi Highway, Siddhicharan Highway, Mid-Hill Highway, and Mechi Highway have been obstructed by landslides.\nSimilarly, in Bagmati Province, the Pasang Lhamu Highway, Araniko Highway, BP Highway, Kanti Lokpath, Madan Bhandari Highway, and Mid-Hill Highway have all been closed.\nPolice have also reported that the Nepal–China border road and the Kulekhani–Sisneri–Dakshinkali–Kathmandu road section are completely blocked.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\ngold\nDashain\nEverest\nsocial media\nUAE\nLandslides\ndisaster\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\n3 hours ago\nNepal Airlines to operate chartered flight from Bhairahawa to Kathmandu today\n4 hours ago\nPM Karki chooses new social media accounts over Oli’s\n4 hours ago\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\n5 hours ago\nKojagrat Purnima: Farewell to Dashain, welcome to Goddess Laxmi\n5 hours ago\nNighttime vehicle movement banned indefinitely on Hetauda–Kathmandu short route\n5 hours ago\nMost Read\nVarious ways you can enjoy goat meat this Dashain festival\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nNepalis celebrate Bijaya Dashami, auspicious Tika time set at 11:53 am\nManaslu climbing in autumn starts on encouraging note; Nima Chhiring sets new record\nMonsoon triggers flood and landslide risks in several districts, DHM issues special alert\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n2 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n2 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n2 months ago\nAlso Read\nDisaster\nNighttime vehicle movement banned indefinitely on Hetauda–Kathmandu short route\n5 hours ago\nDisaster\nHundreds stranded on Everest’s eastern side after heavy snowfall\n8 hours ago\nDisaster\nFloods and landslides obstruct roads at 19 locations in Koshi and Bagmati Provinces\n10 hours ago\nDisaster\nDeath toll from landslides and floods rises to 52 across Nepal\n23 hours ago\nDisaster\nHeavy rain risk eases in Kathmandu Valley, shifts to Koshi Province\n1 day ago",
